       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and single doses are generally capped around 850\u20131,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Extended-release metformin**, for example 1,700 mg once daily with the evening meal\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose, or you can give me a different dose."
      }
